large ship ownership is not very common. aside from the 3 mainly known captains most large vessels are owned by rich merchants. There are smaller ships that come and go owned by large adventuring parties/sailors. There are of course also some decent sized ships owned by more of the pirate types. Those who spend more time stealing from others than searching for treasure themselves. It is possible for players to eventually buy their own vessels. small boats/ships. all the way up to similar sized vessels as the Komatsu or Gullwing. But that takes a large sum of work and coin. Players are more likely to become important members of already established crews. The komatsu plays a large roll in this. As for how advanced the ships are most vessels are very standard ships. mostly for moving cargo. but some are armed. Ships like the Komatsu, Gullwing, and Pandaemonium are armed with all kinds of weaponry and tech that matches the theme of the ship itself. Komatsu is more traditional. Gullwing is more advanced on technology using relics and magic to enhance their ship. While the pandaemonium is much more magic based. It does have standard weaponry but relies more on magic for its tech including flight. Players if they spec into the classes more suited towards it can spend time working on theirs or others ship. weaponry improvement. speed. reinforcement. etc. The sea of swords varies vastly in how dangerous it is. There is a lot of known open space and routes that are mostly safe. But due to the lack of chain of command due to the dragons being gone to help control the natural flow, there are more sea monsters, ghost ships, pirates, etc on the waters. The players will find most of their strange/difficult encounters when they are set of missions, jobs, etc off the normal sailed routes. exploring found caves, investigating ghost ship sightings, following hints on dragons lairs, etc. But while sailing is the primary mode of travel a lot of these destinations are on land, islands, dense uncharted seas, underwater caverns, etc. ship combat is also a thing. being attacked by other vessels while on a journey is a possibility. 
